            "name": "Chatwoot Header Auth"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "parameters": {
          "content": "## Chatwoot AI Agent Bot — setup\n1. **Normalize Event** → set `chatwoot_url` to your Chatwoot base URL.\n2. Create credential **Chatwoot API Token** (Header Auth): name `api_access_token`, value = the Agent Bot token (or a user token). On Chatwoot ≥ 4.19 you can use `Authorization: Bearer <token>` instead.\n3. In Chatwoot create an **Agent Bot** whose Outgoing URL = this webhook's production URL, then attach it to an inbox (Settings → Inboxes → Bot Configuration).\n4. Activate the workflow.\n\nNew conversations in that inbox start as **pending** (bot-owned). The bot only answers while pending; once it calls `handoff_to_human` the status becomes **open** and humans take over.",
          "height": 352,
          "width": 656,
          "color": 4
        },
        "id": "b4d1d8e6-a564-4c1d-a21e-78072c663bf1",
        "name": "Sticky Note 98c5ee12",
        "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
        "typeVersion": 1,
        "position": [
          -16,
          -448
        ]
      },
      {
        "parameters": {
          "content": "### Agent tools (Chatwoot Application API)\n- `reply_to_customer` → POST /messages (outgoing)\n- `add_private_note` → POST /messages (private: true)\n- `set_labels` → POST /labels (overwrites!)\n- `handoff_to_human` → POST /toggle_status {status: open}\nEdit the allowed labels in the set_labels description + system prompt to match your Chatwoot labels.",
          "height": 224,
          "width": 288,
          "color": 5
        },
        "id": "5077e0fd-604d-4bd2-bde3-721019b312d0",
        "name": "Sticky Note e4875351",
